  "summary": "The reviewed documents include several studies applying graph neural network techniques, specifically message passing over relational graphs, to the domain of fraud detection [V0049, V0052, V0051, V0050]. Chen et al. (2020) report the highest performance with an accuracy of 0.94 on the LedgerGuard dataset [V0049]. Fischer et al. (2023) achieved an F1 score of 0.8 on GridWatch [V0052], while El-Sayed et al. (2022) reported an AUROC of 0.73 on ToxiBench [V0051]. Duarte et al. (2021) presented results on CellLife with an MAE of 0.66 [V0050]. Additionally, Chen et al. (2019) applied representation learning techniques to fraudulent transaction identification on GridWatch [V0072].",
